@*
    Media has no component: the module sizes plain img, svg and video elements, so this story shows
    that markup itself on the canvas, where the capture can see it. The empty-state rule only fixes
    the inline size, so its placeholder illustration keeps its own wide aspect; modules.html shows
    the same class on a video instead.
*@
<div class="padding">
    <p class="row">
        <img class="tiny" src="favicon.png" alt="Tiny" />
        <img class="small" src="favicon.png" alt="Small" />
        <img class="medium" src="favicon.png" alt="Medium" />
        <img class="large" src="favicon.png" alt="Large" />
        <img class="extra" src="favicon.png" alt="Extra" />
    </p>
    <p class="row">
        <img class="medium round" src="favicon.png" alt="Round" />
        <img class="medium circle" src="favicon.png" alt="Circle" />
        <img class="medium square" src="favicon.png" alt="Square" />
        <svg class="medium" viewBox="0 0 24 24" role="img" aria-label="Triangle">
            <path d="M12 2 2 22h20z" />
        </svg>
        <video class="medium" poster="favicon.png"></video>
    </p>
    <img class="empty-state" src="empty-state.svg" alt="Empty state" />
    <img class="responsive small" src="favicon.png" alt="Responsive small" />
</div>
